# BUGS

The theme chosen isn't kept: each start puts Platinum Indigo in force, and themes don't yet follow workspaces or apps.
Only the theme's colours are drawn: its materials (gradients, bevels, patterns, shadows), its corners and its typefaces are resolved and served but not drawn, and titles are in the console's 8 by 16 font.
High contrast is a variant to choose, not yet one switch over every theme.
While Radharc reads `/dev/kbd`, the console's shell hears no keys, and nothing else shows its text.
Keys don't repeat, and the keyboard's layout is kbdfs's starting keymap, not a changed one.
Only an image's alpha is blended: a solid layer is opaque, a window has no opacity of its own, and the cursor and titles are drawn in one-bit shapes, so nothing at their edges is blended.
Other transfers and primaries are refused, not converted: the display's colour isn't known, and is taken to be sRGB.
There is no direct scanout, no display driver and no GPU; the screen is the boot framebuffer's size.
The privileged services and secure surfaces are not there yet: a manifest's `grant windows` lines other than `prompt` are refused.
The prompt's `session` and `always` are words for its asker to keep: Radharc records no grant, and the lock screen and the file chooser aren't drawn on the prompt yet.
Its text is in the console's 8 by 16 font.
A key or button held down when the prompt shows never comes up for the window that had it.
The clipboard is at `/svc/windows`, not yet in each window's `/dev`, and there is no drag and drop and no history of entries.
Nothing empties the clipboard but a secret entry's end.
A client killed between two representations of an entry commits the ones it finished.
